Description: R-native implementation of STABL for sparse and reliable biomarker
    discovery. Provides glmnet-based stability selection, FDP+ thresholding,
    artificial-feature controls, grouped bootstrapping, multi-omic early,
    late, and cooperative fusion workflows, visualization helpers, and
    export utilities without a Python or tidymodels runtime dependency. The
    STABL method is described by
    Hédou et al. (2024) <doi:10.1038/s41587-023-02033-x>, and cooperative
    learning by Ding et al. (2022) <doi:10.1073/pnas.2202113119>. The
    cooperative-learning backend (R/cooperative-*.R) is a vendored, modified
    fork of CRAN multiview 1.0 (GPL-2); the full attribution and the
    machine-readable divergence log ship as inst/COPYING.cooperative and
    inst/PATCHES.cooperative.md.
